message: "If you use this playbook, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantum-Safe Migration Playbook (Strategic & Operational Guide)"
abstract: >-
  A Type D Strategic Knowledge Base covering the operational risks of
  migrating enterprise systems to post-quantum cryptography (PQC). Ten
  sections, 42 fact IDs, structured for retrieval-augmented AI ingestion
  and directly usable by human readers. Aligned to NIST FIPS 203 (ML-KEM),
  FIPS 204 (ML-DSA), FIPS 205 (SLH-DSA), NSA CNSA 2.0 timelines, and
  2026 deployment data from Cloudflare and related sources.

  Version 1.2.0 introduces fact-ID structure (§N.M), explicit scope
  boundaries, an expanded evaluation suite with distractor queries, and a
  runtime integration guide with a system prompt ready for ingestion by
  retrieval-augmented AI advisors (e.g., via Kimi K2.5 with the KB-Forge
  toolkit, deposited separately by the same author).

  The playbook covers strategic urgency (CNSA 2.0 timelines, compressed
  Q-Day estimates), current deployment state (hybrid key agreement at
  ~70% of browser-generated traffic, authentication gap), the HNDL threat model, infrastructure impact
  (larger keys/signatures, handshake inflation), hardware bottlenecks
  (HSMs, bootloader trust stores, proprietary ASICs), cryptographic
  discovery (CBOM), skills, pilot design, procurement language, and
  continuous practice.

  Version 1.3.0 adds the M-26-15 filing layer: an agency migration-plan
  template built on OMB Memorandum M-26-15 Appendix B, a federal timeline
  one-pager verified against the primary documents (EO 14412, M-26-15),
  and a filer's checklist for the October 22, 2026 plan deadline.
